        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = -2$: $A = 2$, $B = 1$.<br>Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
